---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const d='/equipment/14-08/',ta='https://www.tainstruments.com/pdf/brochure/BROCH-DSC-2014-EN.pdf',photo='https://www.ite.edu.sg/employers/industry-solutions/facilities-and-equipments/ta-q20-dsc/',dims='https://www.tainstruments.com/pdf/literature/Thermal%20Installation%20Requirements%20Rev%20R.pdf#page=10';
---
<Layout pageTitle="TA Instruments Q20 differential scanning calorimeter" description="Run a virtual DSC scan of an inert synthetic specimen and integrate a thermal transition." wide={true}><article id="q20" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/14-08/">← Equipment 14-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#q20-evidence">Evidence</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">14-08 / HEAT-FLOW CALORIMETRY</p><h2>How much heat did the transition take?</h2><p class="eq-lede">The synthetic specimen crosses a transition at 80 °C. The heat-flow peak gets taller when you double the virtual ramp rate. The integrated energy does not.</p></header>
<div class="q-cols"><section><h3>Q20 manual-pan station</h3><canvas id="dsc-model" aria-label="Orbitable Q20 station; clickable cell lid and pans"></canvas><p id="dsc-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="dsc-front">Full station / reset</button><button id="dsc-cell">Cell close-up</button><button id="dsc-rear">Rear panel</button><p>Click the lid or pans in 3D, or use these controls:</p><p id="dsc-state"></p><button id="dsc-lid">Lift off lid</button><button id="dsc-sample">Remove specimen</button><button id="dsc-ref">Remove reference pan</button></section>
<section><h3>Scan parameters</h3><div class="q-form">{[['mass','Specimen mass, mg',1,25],['cp','Sensible heat capacity, J/(g·K)',.1,3],['energy','Inserted transition enthalpy, J/g',0,100],['temp','Transition center, °C',55,110],['width','Peak half-width, °C',1,8],['rate','Virtual ramp, K/min',1,20],['offset','Synthetic baseline offset, mW',-.5,.5]].map(([id,label,lo,hi])=><label>{label}<input type="number" id={'dsc-'+id} min={lo} max={hi} step="any"/></label>)}<label>Display sign<select id="dsc-sign"><option value="up">Endotherm up</option><option value="down">Endotherm down</option></select></label></div><button id="dsc-run">Run virtual scan</button><button id="dsc-reset">Restore original example</button><p id="dsc-status" role="status"></p><p>Furnace, lid and pans are teaching geometry, not physical setup instructions. No reactor, gas flows or material-specific recipes.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Heat-flow thermogram</h3><label class="q-trace">Plot <select id="dsc-trace"><option value="transition">Corrected transition</option><option value="raw">Specimen, empty reference, and sensible component</option></select></label><canvas id="dsc-chart" width="960" height="355" aria-label="Heat flow in milliwatts versus temperature in degrees Celsius"></canvas><p id="dsc-read" role="status"></p><button id="dsc-json">Download scan JSON</button><button id="dsc-csv">Download trace CSV</button><p>Each row records acquisition time, temperature, specimen/reference/sensible heat flow and the corrected peak. The JSON declares the endotherm convention, sample ID and revision. <a href={d+'example.csv'}>Example CSV</a>.</p></section>
<section id="q20-evidence"><h3>Reference and verification</h3><p>TA Instruments Q-Series Q20 with fixed-position Tzero heat-flux cell and manually removed lid; not an AQ20 autosampler, Q20P pressure instrument, Discovery DSC or optional cooling accessory. Only the published enclosure dimensions are fixed: 460 mm wide × 410 mm tall × 560 mm deep. Lid, pan, tray and connector geometry are inferred. <a href={dims}>TA installation guide, PDF p. 10</a> · <a href={photo}>ITE’s photograph of the manual Q20</a>.</p>
<div class="q-cols q-ref"><figure><img alt="Original Q20 exterior reconstruction" src={d+'station.webp'}/><figcaption>Original exterior view against the ITE photo: blue front cell deck, graphite electronics housing and right-hand convenience tray.</figcaption></figure><figure><img alt="Original open Q20 cell reconstruction" src={d+'cell.webp'}/><figcaption>Original open cell showing paired pans, reconstructed from the <a href={ta+'#page=8'}>manufacturer Tzero sensor illustration, PDF p. 8</a>. Pan dimensions and lid travel are not documented.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>For the virtual demonstration, the instrument baseline is an attributed synthetic drift, and m·C<sub>p</sub>·β is uniform sensible heat flow. Subtract both from specimen flow. The transition is a compact raised cosine of integral one in temperature, scaled by m·Δh·β. Trapezoidal integration over time gives energy in mJ; dividing by mass in mg gives J/g. Gain, sensors, thermal lag and pan mismatch are not mapped to vendor electronics. The scan is simulated, not a material characterization of any named formulation.</p>
<div class="q-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Expected independent result</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>10 mg × 45 J/g = 450 mJ</td><td>450.0 mJ, 45.00 J/g</td><td>0.000001 mJ</td></tr><tr><td>Symmetric peak at 80 °C</td><td>80.00 °C</td><td>One bin, 0.125 °C</td></tr><tr><td>2× ramp gives 2× peak flow, equal integrated energy</td><td>15.00 → 30.00 mW; 450.0 mJ</td><td>0.000001 mW / mJ</td></tr><tr><td>0 inserted transition energy</td><td>No peak; 0.00 J/g</td><td>0.000001 J/g</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'q20.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'calorimetry.mjs'}>Solver and pure state actions</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR ray nodes, bounds and asset budget</a>. No headset or hardware validation claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/14-08/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#q20 .q-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.05fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#q20 section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#q20 .q-form{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.6rem}#q20 label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0}#q20 :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#q20 .q-form :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#q20 button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#q20 button:disabled{opacity:.5}#q20 button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#dsc-model{display:block;width:100%;height:345px;touch-action:none}#dsc-chart{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:#17232b}#dsc-read{font-size:1.25rem}#q20 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#q20 figure img{width:100%}#q20 .q-scroll{max-width:100%;overflow:auto}#q20 table{width:100%;text-align:left;font-size:.9rem}#q20 td,#q20 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem}#q20 .q-trace{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;margin-bottom:.7rem}@media(max-width:760px){#q20 .q-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#dsc-model{height:290px}}</style>
